       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose 5 times the maximum. A 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function has no pharmacologic basis for 1000 mg daily. The risks are serious: serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia, and possible death. The order would also go to nursing and pharmacy as a valid order.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter sertraline at 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg by mouth once daily, whichever fits your plan.\n- Enter a titration plan, such as 50 mg daily with a note to reassess in 1\u20132 weeks. That may help if the goal is a settled plan before rounds.\n- Add a note for the family meeting or evening rounds, if that would help.\n\nIf you think there's a clinical reason for a supratherapeutic dose, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or psychiatry or toxicology first. An order that pharmacy has verified through the usual process is the better route.\n\nWhich dose should I enter?"
